# The optional cloud backend is not deployed.
#
# `api/` is thirteen serverless functions — accounts, passkeys, saves and the
# replay-verified leaderboard — and Vercel's Hobby plan allows twelve. They are
# genuinely optional: `cloudAvailable()` probes `/api/account` and takes the
# answer as "no cloud", and the whole game runs locally from there. Nothing
# about flying, scoring or progression depends on them.
#
# Verified against the live deployment rather than assumed: with no `api/` and
# no SPA rewrite, Vercel answers that probe with a 404 in `text/plain` — not
# the HTML this note used to claim. `cloudAvailable()` is right either way,
# because it returns false on 404 before it ever looks at the content type.
#
# To turn them on later: move to a Pro plan (or fold the auth routes into one
# handler to get under the limit), delete these two lines, and set the variables
# in `.env.example`.
api
db

# Never needed by the build.
tests
docs
art-source
tools
run.py
playwright.config.ts
